::CW_U06_L03_GP_Q01::Story problem: Readers do not understand why Ellis leaves at the end. Which revision best fits?{
~A. Change Ellis's shirt color.#Incorrect. This does not clarify motivation.
~B. Add random weather description.#Incorrect. Weather does not automatically solve character motivation.
=C. Add one action showing Ellis choosing to leave before the final line.#Correct. This directly clarifies motivation and sequence.
~D. Delete every character.#Incorrect. This removes the story instead of revising it.
}

::CW_U06_L03_GP_Q02::Story problem: A suspense scene moves too quickly. Which revision best improves pacing?{
=A. Add action beats as the character listens at the door and watches the light shift.#Correct. Action beats slow the moment and build suspense.
~B. Remove the entire scene.#Incorrect. The scene can be revised.
~C. Add a random joke.#Incorrect. That may weaken suspense.
~D. Change every name.#Incorrect. Names do not control pacing.
}

::CW_U06_L03_GP_Q03::A story shifts accidentally from Mara's thoughts to Ellis's thoughts in the same paragraph. What is the likely problem?{
~A. Setting description.#Incorrect. The issue is not setting.
~B. Spelling only.#Incorrect. The issue is perspective control.
~C. Title length.#Incorrect. The title is not the problem.
=D. Point of view control.#Correct. Accidental shifts in thoughts often create point-of-view confusion.
}

::CW_U06_L03_GP_Q04::Which revision explanation is strongest?{
~A. I changed stuff and now it is better.#Incorrect. This is vague.
=B. I added an action before the ending so readers understand why the character leaves.#Correct. This names the revision and reader effect.
~C. I made the story longer for no reason.#Incorrect. Length alone is not revision quality.
~D. I changed the font.#Incorrect. Font does not explain narrative craft.
}

::CW_U06_L03_GP_Q05::Which story problem should be fixed before final convention polishing?{
~A. One missing comma in an otherwise clear final draft.#Incorrect. That is polishing.
~B. A correctly spelled character name.#Incorrect. That is not a problem.
=C. The central conflict is unclear.#Correct. Major story meaning should be revised before final polish.
~D. A purposeful short sentence.#Incorrect. Purposeful style may not need correction.
}
